{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions","id":1224368,"title":"Crossover questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-03T08:09:00-07:00","id":1224368,"title":"Crossover questions","content":"No, not with the CoD line. This is a bit more out there, a crossover with D&amp;D. I have no idea how this might happen, but that's irrelevant to the question.<br /> <br /> In the default D&amp;D cosmology, Good and Evil are not matters of perspective and point of view. They are not philosophical abstractions. They are fundamental forces of the universe, just as much as gravity and the electric force in our own. So, in this crossover, would the correct arcanum for Detect Good, Magic Circle against Evil, etc. be Primes of Forces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-03T08:18:49-07:00","id":1224369,"title":"","content":"Forces only matters for physical forces, not supernatural ones. If you want to connect the concept to a single Arcanum I'd say Prime. If not, then Fate and Mind could both be used for some of those spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T00:50:11-07:00","id":1224598,"title":"","content":"I imagine you could use Prime to look at their &quot;true&quot; selves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T05:08:29-07:00","id":1224628,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s already objective good and evil in Mage, they exist in the Supernal and are expressed constantly in the Fallen with varying degrees of purity. The arcana simply don\u2019t interact with them in a direct sense. In fact the Paths are only one small imperfect set of lenses through which to view and interact with the Supernal at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T05:40:53-07:00","id":1224640,"title":"","content":"The Supernal is a reflection of the Fallen, and therefore the concepts of good and evil in the Supernal are based on the generally accepted conceptions of good and evil in the Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T05:49:49-07:00","id":1224648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224640#post1224640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Supernal is a reflection of the Fallen, and therefore the concepts of good and evil in the Supernal are based on the generally accepted conceptions of good and evil in the Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the FC perspective, the Diamond perspective is the opposite that the Fallen is an expression of the Supernal.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re probably both right, there\u2019s a feedback loop, and it becomes a chicken egg problem of which came first the Supernal or Fallen.<br /> <br /> Anyway it doesn\u2019t detract from the fact that objective good and evil already exist in Mage, and that Mages have little to no chance of directly interacting with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T12:17:00-07:00","id":1224775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224648#post1224648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway it doesn\u2019t detract from the fact that objective good and evil already exist in Mage, and that Mages have little to no chance of directly interacting with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That the Supernal concepts of good and evil are subjective doesn't detract from the fact that good and evil are objective? What?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T15:14:21-07:00","id":1224820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224775#post1224775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Supernal concepts of good and evil are subjective doesn't detract from the fact that good and evil are objective? What?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure why you\u2019re confused. Reality exists on two levels, the Supernal and the Fallen. Your personal existence exists on two levels, one is the objective fact that you exist and the other is the subjective experience of your existence. The subjective experience is going to affect the objective reality you interact with as you dictate your actions, and vice versa the objective reality is going to affect the kind of subjective experience you can have via the kinds of actions you\u2019re allowed to take.<br /> <br /> The existence of good and evil in Mage is similarly an objective fact because platonic ideals of everything exists in the Supernal. It\u2019s expressed imperfectly into the Fallen in myriad forms. Humans build symbols and platonic ideals from their experiences with good and evil and send those back up the Supernal to influence it in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T15:48:50-07:00","id":1224826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224820#post1224820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m not sure why you\u2019re confused. Reality exists on two levels, the Supernal and the Fallen. Your personal existence exists on two levels, one is the objective fact that you exist and the other is the subjective experience of your existence. The subjective experience is going to affect the objective reality you interact with as you dictate your actions, and vice versa the objective reality is going to affect the kind of subjective experience you can have via the kinds of actions you\u2019re allowed to take.<br /> <br /> The existence of good and evil in Mage is similarly an objective fact because platonic ideals of everything exists in the Supernal. It\u2019s expressed imperfectly into the Fallen in myriad forms. Humans build symbols and platonic ideals from their experiences with good and evil and send those back up the Supernal to influence it in return.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's....a very slippery slope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T16:10:52-07:00","id":1224829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224820#post1224820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure why you\u2019re confused. Reality exists on two levels, the Supernal and the Fallen. Your personal existence exists on two levels, one is the objective fact that you exist and the other is the subjective experience of your existence. The subjective experience is going to affect the objective reality you interact with as you dictate your actions, and vice versa the objective reality is going to affect the kind of subjective experience you can have via the kinds of actions you\u2019re allowed to take.<br /> <br /> The existence of good and evil in Mage is similarly an objective fact because platonic ideals of everything exists in the Supernal. It\u2019s expressed imperfectly into the Fallen in myriad forms. Humans build symbols and platonic ideals from their experiences with good and evil and send those back up the Supernal to influence it in return.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're basically saying is that while good and evil is subjective, the existence of their supernal representations is objective? In the same vein, the existence of your reply in this thread is objective, but the quality and relevance of it is quite subjective?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T16:28:51-07:00","id":1224834,"title":"","content":"Even so, Good, Evil, Law and Chaos are not fundamental forces in CoD cosmology, not in the way they are in a default D&amp;D cosmology, where they're as real and tangible as gravity or the electric force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T18:11:30-07:00","id":1224859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224834#post1224834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, Good, Evil, Law and Chaos are not fundamental forces in CoD cosmology, not in the way they are in a default D&amp;D cosmology, where they're as real and tangible as gravity or the electric force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they are, they just have no direct relationship with the arcana. That doesn\u2019t make them less real.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224829#post1224829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what you're basically saying is that while good and evil is subjective, the existence of their supernal representations is objective? In the same vein, the existence of your reply in this thread is objective, but the quality and relevance of it is quite subjective?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224826#post1224826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's....a very slippery slope.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T04:22:32-07:00","id":1224926,"title":"","content":"They might be real, but they're not.... manifest and tangible as D&amp;D good and evil are. You're really murking the discussion by making points that are only half-relevant to OP's question.<br /> <br /> As for the topic: I'd go with Prime cause that's the Arcanum that governs concepts OR Fate because of how good/evil plays important role is stories, there's always the good guys and bad guys so identifying those would fit Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T05:16:45-07:00","id":1224933,"title":"","content":"Some variant of Soul Marks from the Death Arcana could work.<br /> <br /> Depends what effect these fundamental forces have on the individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T06:19:38-07:00","id":1224939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224926#post1224926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might be real, but they're not.... manifest and tangible as D&amp;D good and evil are. You're really murking the discussion by making points that are only half-relevant to OP's question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, the point I\u2019m making is relevant to the discussion. First, yup good and evil are absolutely manifest and tangible already. Second they exist on a spectrum that Mages can only see from the corner of their eye because the arcana and the Paths don\u2019t directly interact with those symbols.<br /> <br /> Instead of trying to shoehorn the arcana into doing something they\u2019re not supposed to try making something new. This has the additional benefit of being a Mystery rather than saying that the guy with Prime can tell if you\u2019re naughty or nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T07:34:31-07:00","id":1224950,"title":"","content":"No they aren't, you can't talk to beings made of good/evil and make deals with them for instance. Notions of good and evil are in the CoD setting similar to those in the real world.<br /> <br /> And D&amp;D magic can already tell you whether someone is naughty or not. It's a basic spell, and the nature of the duality is well known in the universe. There is no real mystery here as the world is written. And from my understanding the OP isn't looking for a mystery to explore, just for some rules suggestions to play a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T08:24:29-07:00","id":1224959,"title":"","content":"Exactly. I'm considering using a D&amp;D-like setting for a Mage game. This leads to certain necessary questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T09:03:00-07:00","id":1224970,"title":"","content":"Now I think about it, Mage 1e had a very definite morality system. 1e Wisdom has none of the flexibility of 2e; a Mage by virtue of their spiritual state knows what's right and wrong. If I remember right, it's even suggested that they gain no bonus dice for mitigating circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T09:22:34-07:00","id":1224974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224950#post1224950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they aren't, you can't talk to beings made of good/evil and make deals with them for instance. Notions of good and evil are in the CoD setting similar to those in the real world.<br /> <br /> And D&amp;D magic can already tell you whether someone is naughty or not. It's a basic spell, and the nature of the duality is well known in the universe. There is no real mystery here as the world is written. And from my understanding the OP isn't looking for a mystery to explore, just for some rules suggestions to play a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason you can't talk to beings made of good/evil or make deals with them, you just need some in story reason why you can see and communicate with them in the first place. Your view of the Supernal is kind of limited if you think it's purely defined by the ten arcana alone. The 11Q's philosophy for instance is about something sort of like this, that each arcana can answer a particular type of question, but that there's an 11th question that none of the arcana as they're currently known answers.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea that good and evil are similar in CoD to the real world doesn't actually mean anything as a counterargument. Especially, if you're subscribing to the platonic view of reality that Mages have. If there weren't a Supernal Symbol of evil/good then those things wouldn't exist in the Fallen.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point is that you could run a D&amp;D like setting with Mage, but it would require creating some unique facets of the setting. That includes expanding the scope of Supernal magic beyond just the 10 arcana rather than trying to shoehorn the arcana into something they don't normally do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-05-2018, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T09:39:06-07:00","id":1224982,"title":"","content":"Wisdom is actually a good example of the kind of thing I'm talking about. Mages don't really have a direct way of interacting with Wisdom via magic, the closest you can get is via Death by examining, removing, or replacing a soul. There is a platonic ideal of Wisdom in the Supernal, but Mages are typically a fractal expression of it as they exist in the Fallen. The only way to -really- touch Wisdom is to Ascend, but that doesn't make it any less real or make it have any less of an impact on a Mage's existence and experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T09:47:34-07:00","id":1224986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1224959#post1224959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. I'm considering using a D&amp;D-like setting for a Mage game. This leads to certain necessary questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with those who suggest Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T10:16:36-07:00","id":1225000,"title":"","content":"There is nothing wrong with simplyfying things. When someone asks &quot;What's 2+2&quot;, he propably wants &quot;4&quot; as an answer and not &quot;well you haven't specified the numeric system you are using so the question is unanwserable as it is&quot; even though the second one is the more accurate one.<br /> <br /> Nothing wrong with starting a discussion of the philosophical implications, might be interesting even, but then you're going about how people trying to give straight answers have a lesser understanding of the game and are wrong. <br /> <br /> It feels patronizing and annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T11:03:26-07:00","id":1225019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1224368-crossover-questions?p=1225000#post1225000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing wrong with simplyfying things. When someone asks &amp;quot;What's 2+2&amp;quot;, he propably wants &amp;quot;4&amp;quot; as an answer and not &amp;quot;well you haven't specified the numeric system you are using so the question is unanwserable as it is&amp;quot; even though the second one is the more accurate one.<br /> <br /> Nothing wrong with starting a discussion of the philosophical implications, might be interesting even, but then you're going about how people trying to give straight answers have a lesser understanding of the game and are wrong. <br /> <br /> It feels patronizing and annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn\u2019t say it was wrong, or lesser, at worst I said it was limited. Limits aren\u2019t bad if they work. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m pointing out for consideration the fact that objective good/evil are already present in the game. So, while others are trying to shoehorn evil/good into existing arcana, my suggestion is to create something new that interacts with the evil/good that\u2019s already there. The OP can go whatever way they want, but what\u2019s the point of asking if you don\u2019t want different points of view?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T11:11:38-07:00","id":1225022,"title":"","content":"Terms like &quot;shoehorn&quot; or &quot;your view is limited&quot; feel derogatory and usually have negative connotations. Voicing an opinion is well appreciated and as I said, your points are interesting but it's the way they were voiced made be take a defensive stance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T11:19:18-07:00","id":1225025,"title":"","content":"Well, I tried to be as neutral as I know how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}